#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Turn model files (collmodel/5 or /4, from bin/collmodel; --colls and --unit select units) into
an MPICH collective-selection JSON (builder v3, csel_tuner/tree.py).

    bin/colltree bcast.json [bcast_gpu.json] --out bcast_tuning.json [--tol 0.005] [--node-aware]
    bin/colltree run.json [--colls bcast,ibcast] --out tuning.json

Every collective among the selected units gets its subtrees in the one
output file, each built as below from its unit of host buffers and,
optionally, one of device buffers.

Then run with MPIR_CVAR_COLL_SELECTION_JSON_FILE=bcast_tuning.json (and the
collective's algorithm CVAR left at auto). Older model files convert with
bin/collmodel --import.

Each algorithm's model is fitted across layouts from all its curves; a
tree is fitted on the predictions at every point of its layouts x the size
grid, and pruned to the smallest tree whose predicted geomean regret is
within --tol of the full tree's. Without --node-aware it uses comm_size,
msg_size and pof2; --node-aware adds num_nodes and ppn, conditions
MPICH has since pmodels/mpich#8048. Collectives without a message size the
same on every rank (gatherv, scatterv, alltoallv, alltoallw, barrier) do not
split on size: MPICH refuses a file in which they reach msg_size.
--size-condition avg_msg_size writes the older condition, for an MPICH
without msg_size.

One subtree per restriction set (docs/design.md, sections 11 and 12), in
order of increasing mask, so every subset's subtree exists before its
supersets':
- "name=<op>-intra-0", the unrestricted algorithms, on every layout (the
  run-time fallback);
- "name=<op>-intra-<S in hex>", on the layouts where exactly the conditions
  S hold. Its candidates are every algorithm allowed in S as a leaf, and
  "call=" each built subtree of a proper subset of S that uses at least
  --min-fallback-algs algorithms (a smaller one is not worth the call: its
  algorithms are candidates directly). A call is scored at S's own layouts:
  at each point, the predicted time of what that subtree chooses there;
MPICH's built-in call=auto continues in the set of the restrictions that
hold, or its largest present subset (restrictions are positive, so whatever a
subset allows is allowed there too; at worst set 0). A set reaches a subset's
subtree with "call=auto(<mask>)", leaving out the restrictions of the
collective's sets that the subset lacks, since MPICH allows call= only to free
names; two sets of the same size that could both match a call are refused by
MPICH, so colltree adds their union as an alias to the one the legacy dispatch
used. With --format legacy, for an MPICH without the reserved names:
"name=<op>-intra-auto", the dispatch: "dispatch=<op>-intra(<bits>)" (the
restriction-mask node of pmodels/mpich#8048), or with --nested-dispatch nested
restrictive conditions ending in "call=" the subtrees; sets call each other by
name.

Several variant units of one collective and memory kind (in-place and
not; the reductions' builtin commutative op) share its subtrees: each
unit's input conditions are set in all its masks (variant_base), its base
set covers every layout, and a set may call a subset's subtree from another
variant, scored with this unit's own curves. Without a variant free of
input conditions, the one with the fewest builds set 0 from its
unrestricted algorithms.

Several models, one per memory kind of the buffers (a model's "mem": host,
or gpu from bin/collmodel --launch gpu), go into one file. The two device
conditions shape the file differently, because all ranks of a call must reach
the same algorithm:

- gpu_coll is the same on all ranks, so it selects subtrees of their own: the
  gpu model's, the -gpu variant "name=<op>-intra-<S in hex>-gpu", in which
  call=auto falls back within the variant (to "<op>-intra-0-gpu"), and only if
  none matches to the host sets. Both conditions hold in the whole model, so they
  are left out of S and of the algorithms' restrictions (an algorithm restricted
  to gpu alone, e.g. buffer_swap, is unrestricted there).
- gpu_local can differ between ranks, so MPICH takes it through a local set
  first, "name=<op>-intra-<gpu_local bit>" (e.g. -400), whose leaves are
  buffer_swap, which clears the flags and selects again, or "call=auto(<that
  bit>)", where the host ranks go. A device call without gpu_coll therefore runs
  the host sets' algorithm, directly or after a swap, and a gpu_coll call never
  takes the local set. Where the gpu model predicts buffer_swap faster than the
  host sets' choice at some point, the file has the local set. Above
  --guard-above the choice is not to swap, and a point whose algorithm has no
  curve in the gpu model is reported and not counted. MPICH does not define
  gpu_coll for gatherv, scatterv and alltoallv, so they have no gpu sets: their
  gpu model only serves the swap choice. (--format legacy: the choice is
  "name=<op>-intra-main": {"gpu_coll": "call=auto", "gpu_local": <the choice>,
  "any": "call=auto"}, which "name=main" sends the collective to, and the gpu
  subtrees are "<op>-intra-gpu-<S>" with a dispatch of their own, under
  {"gpu_coll": <gpu dispatch>, "any": <host dispatch>}.)

A more restricted tree is written only if it is unique: a subtree that chooses like
its fallback at every point it was fitted on, and the gpu subtrees if they choose
like the host sets and the swap choice at every point of the gpu models. These are
reported. The inner calls of a compositional algorithm select with call=auto and the
flags they inherit, so on device buffers they can reach the local set (legacy: from
auto, so only a user's call swaps, in main).

A host model is required; each memory kind at most once.

A compositional algorithm (e.g. smp) was measured with a tuning file
selecting its inner calls. Where the output chooses it, colltree compares
the output's choices for those inner calls (on the node communicator, the
node leaders' communicator or the caller's own, into any collective whose
tree is in the output: smp's bcast, nb's ibcast, buffer_swap's host tree)
with that file's, and lists where they differ by more than --stale-tol in
predicted time, by the inner collective's model: there the measurements
are stale, and the algorithm should be measured again with the output
loaded (bin/collmodel --model ... --algs smp --inner-selection <output>).
"""
